assistant secretary at the Department

3500
04:44:41,411 --> 04:44:47,723
of Health and Human Services in August. It was still
there in October. It was still there

3501
04:44:47,743 --> 04:44:53,914
in December. It was never rejected. It was simply
never read, by a department that had,

3502
04:44:53,934 --> 04:45:00,104
that summer, accepted a three-hundred-million-dollar
grant from the Umbrella Foundation

3503
04:45:00,124 --> 04:45:06,295
to build rural health clinics in six states, and was
planning a ribbon-cutting with the

3504
04:45:06,315 --> 04:45:08,073
Secretary for the spring.

3505
04:45:08,643 --> 04:45:14,987
Nobody had told the deputy assistant secretary to sit
on it. That was the art of it. Nobody

3506
04:45:15,007 --> 04:45:20,930
ever needs to be told. They only need to be able to
imagine what might happen if they

3507
04:45:20,950 --> 04:45:21,419
didn't.

3508
04:45:23,609 --> 04:45:30,195
You have made a policeman into a joke and a doctor
into an unread file. Without a single

3509
04:45:30,215 --> 04:45:30,720
threat.

3510
04:45:31,241 --> 04:45:33,589
Threats leave fingerprints. Budgets don't.

3511
04:45:34,109 --> 04:45:37,353
In my day, we would simply have
arrested them.

3512
04:45:37,873 --> 04:45:43,676
In your day, the people you arrested became martyrs,
and the martyrs became a resistance,

3513
04:45:43,696 --> 04:45:49,695
and the resistance became a problem you had to solve
with more arrests. I prefer my problems

3514
04:45:49,715 --> 04:45:51,004
to solve themselves.

3515
04:45:53,024 --> 04:45:57,617
In the middle of it all, almost as an
afterthought, Aeterna was approved.

3516
04:45:58,186 --> 04:46:04,295
The Food and Drug Administration granted full
approval on the eighteenth of June, twenty

3517
04:46:04,315 --> 04:46:10,285
thirty, for the treatment of age-related frailty in
adults over sixty-five. It was the

3518
04:46:10,305 --> 04:46:16,692
fastest approval of a new molecular entity in the
agency's history. At the press conference,

3519
04:46:16,712 --> 04:46:23,100
Arthur Kowalczyk, eighty-one years old, stood up in the
front row, and when the Commissioner

3520
04:46:23,120 --> 04:46:29,229
said the word approved, he punched the air like a man
at a ball game, and the photograph

3521
04:46:29,249 --> 04:46:35,149
of him doing it was on the front page of every
newspaper in America the next morning.

3522
04:46:35,719 --> 04:46:42,163
Within a year, Aeterna would be prescribed to four
million Americans. Within three, forty

3523
04:46:42,183 --> 04:46:48,773
million people worldwide. It would reduce hospital
admissions among the elderly by a third.

3524
04:46:48,793 --> 04:46:54,802
It would be, by any honest measure, one of the
most beneficial medicines ever made.

3525
04:46:55,371 --> 04:47:01,199
That is the part of this story that is hardest to
hold in your mind at the same time as

3526
04:47:01,219 --> 04:47:07,247
the rest of it. So hold it anyway. It was true.
Millions of people lived longer, healthier

3527
04:47:07,267 --> 04:47:11,145
lives because of a man who did not
care about them at all.

3528
04:47:13,965 --> 04:47:17,493
Assessment. Market dominance, global.

3529
04:47:21,690 --> 04:47:23,122
Level twenty-six.

3530
04:47:27,181 --> 04:47:30,312
Purchase confirmed. Memory palace.

3531
04:47:34,051 --> 04:47:39,762
The Memory Palace had to be built. The System said
so, in a line of small text beneath

3532
04:47:39,782 --> 04:47:45,427
the purchase — the structure is determined by the
Host — and so, that night, lying on

3533
04:47:45,447 --> 04:47:51,358
his back in the dark in the bare apartment on the
riverfront where he slept perhaps three

3534
04:47:51,378 --> 04:47:53,157
hours a night, he built it.

3535
04:47:53,727 --> 04:47:57,813
It was the first real argument they had
had about architecture.

3536
04:47:59,502 --> 04:48:05,930
A palace should be a palace. Columns. Marble. A
great hall. A chancellery. Rooms that

3537
04:48:05,950 --> 04:48:09,039
make the men who walk in them feel small.

3538
04:48:09,559 --> 04:48:10,903
It's a filing system.

3539
04:48:11,424 --> 04:48:17,079
It is the inside of your mind. You will live in it
more than you live in your body. Make

3540
04:48:17,099 --> 04:48:19,788
it worthy of what you are going to become.

3541
04:48:21,507 --> 04:48:27,465
Wesker did not answer at once. And when he did, it
was not an argument. It was simply

3542
04:48:27,485 --> 04:48:32,316
a decision, made quietly, the way he made
all the ones that mattered.

3543
04:48:32,886 --> 04:48:35,010
He built it as the old building.

3544
04:48:35,578 --> 04:48:42,099
Four storeys of tired brick. A lobby with a water
stain. A break room with a humming vending

3545
04:48:42,119 --> 04:48:48,214
machine and an old piano in the corner. A corner
office with a leather chair. And then

3546
04:48:48,234 --> 04:48:54,470
— because it was a mind, and minds do not have to
obey geology — corridors that went on,

3547
04:48:54,490 --> 04:49:00,940
and on, beyond the walls, down stairs that did not
exist, into floors beneath the basement,

3548
04:49:00,960 --> 04:49:07,125
each corridor lined with doors, and behind every
door, a person. Every face he had ever

3549
04:49:07,145 --> 04:49:10,823
read. Every file. Every
conversation, word for word.

3550
04:49:11,393 --> 04:49:17,099
Walter Pruitt had a door on the ground floor, by
the security booth. Hannah Price had

3551
04:49:17,119 --> 04:49:21,277
one in the basement, beside a freezer.
Owen Carrick had three.

3552
04:49:21,967 --> 04:49:23,780
You made it the building.

3553
04:49:24,300 --> 04:49:29,441
It's the only place I've ever started from nothing.
I'd like to remember what that was

3554
04:49:29,461 --> 04:49:29,741
like.

3555
04:49:31,762 --> 04:49:37,716
The Adolf half of the mind said nothing for a long
time. And then, very quietly, in a

3556
04:49:37,736 --> 04:49:43,971
room on the fourth floor of an imaginary building
that only one skull contained, it asked

3557
04:49:43,991 --> 04:49:49,944
for a door of its own. And Wesker, after a moment,
gave it one — on the fourth floor,

3558
04:49:49,964 --> 04:49:53,598
at the end of a corridor, with no
name on it at all.

3559
04:49:55,669 --> 04:50:01,562
On the second of September, at seven in the morning,
a black SUV with government plates

3560
04:50:01,582 --> 04:50:06,389
pulled into the visitors' bay of the
Umbrella tower, and a man got out.

3561
04:50:06,958 --> 04:50:12,487
He was lean, somewhere in his late fifties, with
silver hair and a navy suit and no tie,

3562
04:50:12,507 --> 04:50:17,910
and the kind of face that has spent a long career
being forgettable on purpose. He did

3563
04:50:17,930 --> 04:50:23,396
not have an appointment. He walked into the lobby,
past the living wall, past the Creed

3564
04:50:23,416 --> 04:50:28,818
in its small elegant letters, to the reception desk,
where a receptionist who had once

3565
04:50:28,838 --> 04:50:33,926
been a Common roll in a basement ten-pull looked
up at him with perfect courtesy.

3566
04:50:34,616 --> 04:50:39,283
Good morning. My name's Martin Sloane. I'd like to
see Doctor Wesker, please. Tell him

3567
04:50:39,303 --> 04:50:40,591
I'm from the government.

3568
04:50:41,590 --> 04:50:42,804
The other part of it.

3569
04:50:44,823 --> 04:50:50,452
The receptionist did not ask which part. She did
not need to. She picked up a phone.

3570
04:50:51,021 --> 04:50:57,175
On the twelfth floor, in a corner office with a view of
the river, Albert Wesker had watched

3571
04:50:57,195 --> 04:51:03,012
the black SUV arrive on the security feed. He had
watched the man get out, and walk in,

3572
04:51:03,032 --> 04:51:08,716
and put the card on the desk. And the Cold-Read,
even through a security camera, even

3573
04:51:08,736 --> 04:51:14,553
from twelve floors away, had shown him everything he
needed to know about Martin Sloane

3574
04:51:14,573 --> 04:51:15,492
in one glance.

3575
04:51:16,063 --> 04:51:22,098
Curiosity. Ambition. Contempt for rules. And
beneath it all, like the steady light of

3576
04:51:22,118 --> 04:51:28,224
a pilot flame, something he had not seen in any of
the three. Something he recognised,

3577
04:51:28,244 --> 04:51:31,501
because he saw it every morning
in the mirror.

3578
04:51:32,072 --> 04:51:33,125
Appetite.

3579
04:51:49,569 --> 04:51:55,129
Martin Sloane did not waste time. It was the first
thing the Director liked about him.

3580
04:51:55,818 --> 04:52:00,862
I'm not here to investigate you, Doctor Wesker. I
want to be clear about that. The Bureau

3581
04:52:00,882 --> 04:52:05,697
does that. The Bureau is very bad at it, as you've
noticed. My part of the government

3582
04:52:05,717 --> 04:52:07,574
doesn't investigate. It collects.

3583
04:52:08,094 --> 04:52:09,398
And what are you collecting?

3584
04:52:09,916 --> 04:52:13,947
Information. About people who are about to try
to take something from you.

3585
04:52:15,348 --> 04:52:20,785
Since January, we've been hearing a word in some very
interesting places. In Moscow, mostly.

3586
04:52:20,805 --> 04:52:25,828
In some traffic between people who work for a
certain service, and people who used to

3587
04:52:25,848 --> 04:52:30,871
work for a certain private military company that
the Kremlin likes to pretend doesn't

3588
04:52:30,891 --> 04:52:35,914
exist. The word is Umbrella. Sometimes they also
use a word that translates, roughly,

3589
04:52:35,934 --> 04:52:36,447
as ghost.

3590
04:52:36,968 --> 04:52:38,152
They've seen the video.

3591
04:52:38,672 --> 04:52:44,153
Everybody's seen the video. The difference is that some
people watched it and saw a rolling-shutter

3592
04:52:44,173 --> 04:52:47,154
artefact, and some people watched it
and saw a weapon.

3593
04:52:48,673 --> 04:52:50,381
And which did you see, Mister Sloane?

3594
04:52:52,402 --> 04:52:58,571
Sloane smiled. It was a thin, cold, genuinely
amused smile, and the Cold-Read read it

3595
04:52:58,591 --> 04:53:00,974
with something close to pleasure.

3596
04:53:01,663 --> 04:53:06,321
I saw a man who doesn't want to be collected by the
Russians. I'm here to suggest that

3597
04:53:06,341 --> 04:53:08,225
you'd prefer to be collected by us.

3598
04:53:09,744 --> 04:53:15,407
He left a telephone number on a plain white card,
and a warning, and nothing else. He

3599
04:53:15,427 --> 04:53:19,151
did not ask for anything. That, too,
the Director liked.

3600
04:53:21,342 --> 04:53:23,746
The Americans want to own you.

3601
04:53:24,265 --> 04:53:29,440
The Americans want to rent me. There's a difference.
And the Russians want to steal me.

3602
04:53:29,460 --> 04:53:34,516
Which means that, for the first time, someone is
going to come at us who isn't afraid

3603
04:53:34,536 --> 04:53:35,352
of the police.

3604
04:53:35,872 --> 04:53:37,495
Then let them come.

3605
04:53:38,013 --> 04:53:39,289
Yes. I think we should.

3606
04:53:40,810 --> 04:53:43,463
You are thinking of the creature.

3607
04:53:43,982 --> 04:53:49,637
I'm thinking that I own a weapon I've never seen used.
I'm thinking that a Russian contractor

3608
04:53:49,657 --> 04:53:55,007
team is the only enemy on Earth I could use it on
that nobody would ever report missing.

3609
04:53:55,027 --> 04:54:00,376
And I'm thinking that it's been asleep for four
years, and I'd like to know what it does

3610
04:54:00,396 --> 04:54:01,413
when it wakes up.

3611
04:54:03,433 --> 04:54:09,347
The Adolf half of the mind was silent for a long
moment. When it spoke, its voice had

3612
04:54:09,367 --> 04:54:15,350
changed — lower, slower, and with something in it
that the Wesker half had never quite

3613
04:54:15,370 --> 04:54:19,189
heard before. Not joy. Something
more careful than joy.

3614
04:54:19,880 --> 04:54:25,826
You have always told me to wait. Not yet. Not yet.
You told the girl at the piano. You

3615
04:54:25,846 --> 04:54:27,838
told the creature in the ice.

3616
04:54:28,358 --> 04:54:29,063
I did.

3617
04:54:29,583 --> 04:54:30,672
And now?

3618
04:54:31,193 --> 04:54:33,006
Now it's a controlled experiment.

3619
04:54:35,657 --> 04:54:38,958
Purchase confirmed. Desert complex.

3620
04:54:43,832 --> 04:54:49,594
The facility appeared in the Mojave Desert in the
second week of October, forty miles

3621
04:54:49,614 --> 04:54:55,376
from the nearest town, on land that an Ashford
Pacific subsidiary had bought from the

3622
04:54:55,396 --> 04:54:59,321
Bureau of Land Management two years
before and never used.

3623
04:54:59,892 --> 04:55:06,221
On the surface, it was a data centre. Low concrete
buildings, a fence, a row of cooling

3624
04:55:06,241 --> 04:55:12,497
units, a microwave mast. It even held data — real
servers, running real workloads, for

3625
04:55:12,517 --> 04:55:18,773
real customers, at a loss. Below the surface, four
levels down, it was something else.

3626
04:55:19,344 --> 04:55:25,104
They moved the Tyrant out of Wilmington on a moonless
night, in a refrigerated truck with

3627
04:55:25,124 --> 04:55:30,626
the name of a produce company on its side, escorted
by four of the Silent Ones in two

3628
04:55:30,646 --> 04:55:36,212
black cars, across two thousand four hundred miles
of interstate. Evelyn Marsh rode in

3629
04:55:36,232 --> 04:55:41,928
the cab. She had insisted. She had not left the
cradle's side for four years and she was

3630
04:55:41,948 --> 04:55:44,981
not, she told the Director,
going to start now.

3631
04:55:45,551 --> 04:55:51,717
It arrived on the third day, and was lowered into the
deepest level of the desert complex,

3632
04:55:51,737 --> 04:55:55,566
and bolted down. Its breathing, in
the new room, echoed.

3633
04:55:57,636 --> 04:56:01,829
And then — carefully, over three weeks — he
let the Russians find it.

3634
04:56:02,399 --> 04:56:08,065
It was not difficult. Ashford Pacific's logistics
system had been under quiet attack from

3635
04:56:08,085 --> 04:56:13,752
a group in Saint Petersburg since the spring; Hale's
people had noticed in April and done

3636
04:56:13,772 --> 04:56:19,310
nothing, on the Director's instructions, except
watch. Now, in the shipping records the

3637
04:56:19,330 --> 04:56:25,380
hackers were reading, a single line appeared. A transfer
of biological material, classification

3638
04:56:25,400 --> 04:56:31,067
restricted, from Wilmington to a data centre in
Nevada. Handling instructions: cryogenic.

3639
04:56:31,087 --> 04:56:32,473
Security escort: four.

3640
04:56:33,043 --> 04:56:36,490
Four. It was a very small number.
It was meant to be.

3641
04:56:38,560 --> 04:56:43,283
They came on the nineteenth of November, at four
minutes past two in the morning.

3642
04:56:43,854 --> 04:56:49,451
There were twelve of them. They had come into the
country separately, over two weeks,

3643
04:56:49,471 --> 04:56:55,333
on real passports, through four different airports,
and assembled in a rented ranch house

3644
04:56:55,353 --> 04:57:01,281
outside Barstow. They were former soldiers of the
Russian special forces, and of a private

3645
04:57:01,301 --> 04:57:07,229
company that had fought in Syria, and Libya, and Mali,
and Ukraine. They had night vision,

3646
04:57:07,249 --> 04:57:13,309
and suppressed rifles, and a drone, and a thermal lance
for the vault door, and a helicopter

3647
04:57:13,329 --> 04:57:18,992
waiting fifteen miles away with a pilot who had
flown for three different governments.

3648
04:57:19,563 --> 04:57:25,006
They were, by any standard, the most dangerous group
of people who had ever tried to take

3649
04:57:25,026 --> 04:57:26,725
anything from Albert Wesker.

3650
04:57:27,294 --> 04:57:33,511
He watched them come, from a control room four levels
down, on a wall of screens. Evelyn

3651
04:57:33,531 --> 04:57:36,416
stood beside him. Hale stood by the door.

3652
04:57:37,106 --> 04:57:40,073
Fence is down. Two guards at the
east door. Moving.

3653
04:57:40,592 --> 04:57:46,261
The two guards at the east door were Silent Ones.
They had been told to step aside. They

3654
04:57:46,281 --> 04:57:52,078
stepped aside, with perfect courtesy, and the twelve
men went past them without ever quite

3655
04:57:52,098 --> 04:57:54,986
seeing them, and into the
building, and down.

3656
04:57:57,056 --> 04:58:02,798
At the fourth level, in front of a steel door with a
red-and-white emblem painted on it,

3657
04:58:02,818 --> 04:58:06,073
the team leader raised his hand,
and they stopped.

3658
04:58:06,642 --> 04:58:11,601
And four levels down, in the control room,
Albert Wesker said two words.

3659
04:58:13,293 --> 04:58:14,019
Wake it.

3660
04:58:16,539 --> 04:58:22,399
In the deepest room of the desert complex, for the
first time in four years, the cradle

3661
04:58:22,419 --> 04:58:22,873
opened.

3662
04:58:25,943 --> 04:58:27,985
The team saw it first on thermal.

3663
04:58:28,674 --> 04:58:32,856
Contact. Contact, front. Something big. Very
hot. Very — it's very big.

3664
04:58:33,255 --> 04:58:34,281
Is that a man?

3665
04:58:35,681 --> 04:58:36,726
That's not a man.

3666
04:58:37,745 --> 04:58:43,435
They opened fire. They were professionals, and they
did it well — four rifles at once,

3667
04:58:43,455 --> 04:58:49,277
controlled bursts, aimed at the centre of mass. The
corridor filled with light and noise

3668
04:58:49,297 --> 04:58:50,937
and the smell of cordite.

3669
04:58:51,507 --> 04:58:57,854
It did not stop. It did not hurry, either. It walked
into the gunfire the way a man walks

3670
04:58:57,874 --> 04:58:58,570
into rain.

3671
04:59:00,640 --> 04:59:06,093
What happened in the next ninety seconds, the
Director watched on the wall of screens

3672
04:59:06,113 --> 04:59:11,695
with his arms folded, and Evelyn Marsh watched
beside him with a notebook, writing, and

3673
04:59:11,715 --> 04:59:16,074
Hale watched by the door, and none of the
three of them looked away.

3674
04:59:16,644 --> 04:59:22,316
The narrator will not describe it. Not because it
cannot be described — but because the

3675
04:59:22,336 --> 04:59:28,009
men in that corridor were somebody's sons, and they
had come to steal, and they did not

3676
04:59:28,029 --> 04:59:33,636
deserve to be remembered only as the first people on
this Earth to learn what a Tyrant

3677
04:59:33,656 --> 04:59:34,159
was for.

3678
04:59:37,729 --> 04:59:42,048
It took ninety seconds. The radio chatter
lasted seventy of them.

3679
04:59:42,738 --> 04:59:45,032
Fall back! Fall back to the — it's
in the — oh God —

3680
04:59:47,551 --> 04:59:48,829
And then it didn't.

3681
04:59:50,899 --> 04:59:57,143
Twenty miles away, a helicopter pilot who had flown for
three different governments listened

3682
04:59:57,163 --> 05:00:03,202
to his radio go silent, and waited exactly as long as
his training said to wait, and then

3683
05:00:03,222 --> 05:00:08,989
lifted off, alone, and flew south toward the
Mexican border, and was never heard from

3684
05:00:09,009 --> 05:00:11,508
again by anyone who had employed him.

3685
05:00:14,578 --> 05:00:17,646
In the control room, nobody
spoke for a while.

3686
05:00:18,217 --> 05:00:24,030
Evelyn finished writing. She closed her notebook, and
held it against her chest with both

3687
05:00:24,050 --> 05:00:30,126
arms, and looked at the wall of screens, where a
nine-foot grey figure was standing perfectly

3688
05:00:30,146 --> 05:00:35,370
still at the end of a smoke-filled corridor,
waiting to be told what to do next.

3689
05:00:36,059 --> 05:00:37,010
It was perfect.

3690
05:00:38,529 --> 05:00:42,795
Hale said nothing. Hale never said
anything he had not been asked.

3691
05:00:43,366 --> 05:00:49,051
The Director stood with his arms folded, and looked
at the screen, and did not move for

3692
05:00:49,071 --> 05:00:49,837
a long time.

3693
05:00:52,028 --> 05:00:53,565
Do you see it now?

3694
05:00:54,085 --> 05:00:54,876
I see it.

3695
05:00:55,395 --> 05:01:01,757
Twelve soldiers. The best Russia has. Ninety seconds.
One of them. Do you understand what

3696
05:01:01,777 --> 05:01:04,912
we could do with a hundred?
With a thousand?

3697
05:01:05,432 --> 05:01:06,841
I understand exactly.

3698
05:01:07,361 --> 05:01:14,245
An army of these. Not in a desert. In the streets of a
capital. At the gates of a parliament.

3699
05:01:14,265 --> 05:01:20,183
No one could stand against it. No one. Not the
Americans, not the Chinese, not —

3700
05:01:20,703 --> 05:01:21,385
Stop.

3701
05:01:23,404 --> 05:01:29,256
It was the first time Wesker had ever told the other
voice to stop. It was not a request.

3702
05:01:29,946 --> 05:01:34,811
An army of these is a war. Listen to me. A war. With
the whole world. Tomorrow. Against

3703
05:01:34,831 --> 05:01:39,864
every government on this planet, all at once, united —
for the first time in their history

3704
05:01:39,884 --> 05:01:44,637
— by the one thing they will all agree on, which is
that we have to be destroyed. You

3705
05:01:44,657 --> 05:01:48,849
know how that ends. You were there. You ended
it in a bunker with a pistol.

3706
05:01:49,369 --> 05:01:51,418
I did not have this.

3707
05:01:51,938 --> 05:01:57,261
You had the best army in Europe and the world took
it apart in six years. Because they

3708
05:01:57,281 --> 05:02:02,543
saw you coming. Because you showed them. That's the
only lesson either of us was ever

3709
05:02:02,563 --> 05:02:03,661
