3731
05:03:52,650 --> 05:03:58,250
into it without being told, as if it had simply
been waiting for permission to sleep.

3732
05:03:58,819 --> 05:04:04,447
Evelyn Marsh sat on the floor of the cold room in
front of the window until morning, with

3733
05:04:04,467 --> 05:04:06,477
her palm flat against the glass.

3734
05:04:07,048 --> 05:04:13,549
There were no bodies. There was nothing to find. By
the time the sun rose over the Mojave,

3735
05:04:13,569 --> 05:04:19,708
the fourth level of the desert complex was clean,
and quiet, and smelled only faintly

3736
05:04:19,728 --> 05:04:21,158
of cordite and cold.

3737
05:04:21,726 --> 05:04:27,910
Twelve men had come to steal something. The world
never learned what had happened to them.

3738
05:04:27,930 --> 05:04:33,837
Their families, in Moscow and Rostov and Krasnodar,
were told that they had died in an

3739
05:04:33,857 --> 05:04:35,146
accident in Africa.

3740
05:04:53,406 --> 05:04:59,221
In the third week of January, in a windowless room on
the fourth floor of a green-and-cream

3741
05:04:59,241 --> 05:05:04,864
building beside the Thames, five people sat down
around a table to talk about a company.

3742
05:05:05,434 --> 05:05:10,940
None of them would ever admit that the meeting had
taken place. There was no agenda, no

3743
05:05:10,960 --> 05:05:17,101
minutes, and no name on the booking. There were only five
liaison officers from five intelligence

3744
05:05:17,121 --> 05:05:22,691
services — British, German, French, American, and
Dutch — who had each, separately, over

3745
05:05:22,711 --> 05:05:28,408
the preceding year, noticed something about Umbrella
Life Sciences that did not sit right,

3746
05:05:28,428 --> 05:05:33,680
and who had each, separately, been told by their
own governments to leave it alone.

3747
05:05:34,250 --> 05:05:39,790
The meeting was chaired by a man named Julian
Ashcombe. He was fifty-four, patrician,

3748
05:05:39,810 --> 05:05:45,349
patient, and dressed as though it were still
nineteen fifty-five. He had spent thirty

3749
05:05:45,369 --> 05:05:51,039
years in the Secret Intelligence Service, most of
them in places where patience was the

3750
05:05:51,059 --> 05:05:56,795
only weapon that did not get you killed. He was, by
the unanimous judgment of the people

3751
05:05:56,815 --> 05:06:02,616
who had worked against him, the most dangerous man in
the room, and he was always, always

3752
05:06:02,636 --> 05:06:03,074
polite.

3753
05:06:03,763 --> 05:06:06,060
Shall we begin with the patents?

3754
05:06:08,079 --> 05:06:10,736
The patents were the German contribution.

3755
05:06:11,305 --> 05:06:17,564
The Federal Intelligence Service in Berlin employed
a small unit whose only job was to

3756
05:06:17,584 --> 05:06:24,280
watch the world's patent offices for signs of
technological surprise — the sudden appearance

3757
05:06:24,300 --> 05:06:30,485
of an idea that should, by any normal measure, have
taken a decade to arrive. In four

3758
05:06:30,505 --> 05:06:36,763
years, Umbrella Life Sciences had filed four hundred
and eighteen patents. Sixty-three

3759
05:06:36,783 --> 05:06:43,698
of them, the German analysts had concluded, described
inventions with no traceable intellectual

3760
05:06:43,718 --> 05:06:50,487
ancestry. No preceding papers. No conference talks. No
doctoral theses. No failed experiments

3761
05:06:50,507 --> 05:06:56,765
by other groups. They had simply appeared, fully
formed, as if someone had been handed

3762
05:06:56,785 --> 05:06:57,641
the answers.

3763
05:06:58,331 --> 05:07:03,933
In science, ideas have parents. Sixty-three of these
are orphans. That is not statistically

3764
05:07:03,953 --> 05:07:09,246
possible. Either Umbrella has the best research team
