3904
05:18:40,772 --> 05:18:46,574
on weekends, and on the vacation days he had been
saving for a trip to Disney World that

3905
05:18:46,594 --> 05:18:50,212
his daughters no longer mentioned,
he watched Umbrella.

3906
05:18:50,782 --> 05:18:55,508
It was Samira Haddad who found the way
in. Not a door. The air.

3907
05:18:56,078 --> 05:19:01,775
A laboratory of the highest containment grade breathes
in a particular way. It keeps itself

3908
05:19:01,795 --> 05:19:07,241
at negative pressure, so that nothing inside can
leak out; it pulls its exhaust through

3909
05:19:07,261 --> 05:19:12,581
two stages of very fine filters, and it pushes that
exhaust out through a stack, high

3910
05:19:12,601 --> 05:19:18,172
above the ground, at a steady rate that never varies,
day or night, weekends or holidays.

3911
05:19:18,192 --> 05:19:23,512
It is the heartbeat of the thing. You cannot hide
it, because if you ever stopped it,

3912
05:19:23,532 --> 05:19:25,648
whatever was inside would get out.

3913
05:19:26,337 --> 05:19:31,182
The old building has four exhaust stacks on the
roof. Three are what you'd expect for

3914
05:19:31,202 --> 05:19:36,046
a building that size. The fourth is too big. It
runs twenty-four hours a day. I had a

3915
05:19:36,066 --> 05:19:40,967
colleague look at the thermal imagery from the
state's aerial survey. It's warmer than

3916
05:19:40,987 --> 05:19:43,542
the others, and steadier, and
it never stops.

3917
05:19:44,061 --> 05:19:45,520
And if we could sample it?

3918
05:19:46,040 --> 05:19:50,718
Then I could tell you whether there's a grade-four
lab under that building. I couldn't

3919
05:19:50,738 --> 05:19:53,505
tell you what's in it. But I could
prove it exists.

3920
05:19:55,525 --> 05:20:02,038
It was, all three of them knew, a crime. Trespass,
at the least. For an FBI agent, the

3921
05:20:02,058 --> 05:20:05,457
end of a career. For a CDC
officer, the same.

3922
05:20:06,027 --> 05:20:11,465
They did it anyway, on the night of the eleventh of
April, because they had run out of

3923
05:20:11,485 --> 05:20:12,924
legal ways to be right.

3924
05:20:14,995 --> 05:20:20,771
They went up the fire escape at the back of the old
building at twenty to two in the morning.

3925
05:20:20,791 --> 05:20:26,131
Haddad carried a portable air sampler in a backpack.
Carrick carried his Bureau-issued

3926
05:20:26,151 --> 05:20:31,615
pistol, which he was not supposed to have on him
outside of duty hours, and which he had

3927
05:20:31,635 --> 05:20:34,544
brought without quite admitting
to himself why.

3928
05:20:35,115 --> 05:20:36,496
Nobody stopped them.

3929
05:20:37,067 --> 05:20:42,420
That should have told them something. Afterwards,
it did. There were six men in black

3930
05:20:42,440 --> 05:20:48,110
on the Umbrella campus that night. There were cameras
on every corner of the old building.

3931
05:20:48,130 --> 05:20:53,548
And two amateurs with a backpack climbed a fire
escape in plain sight, and reached the

3932
05:20:53,568 --> 05:20:55,254
roof, and nothing happened.

3933
05:20:55,824 --> 05:21:01,224
Haddad went straight to the fourth stack and set up
the sampler. It took nine minutes.

3934
05:21:01,244 --> 05:21:06,581
Carrick stood watch at the edge of the roof with
his back to her, looking down at the

3935
05:21:06,601 --> 05:21:11,873
empty parking lot where frame one thousand one
hundred and fourteen had been filmed.

3936
05:21:12,564 --> 05:21:18,985
Owen. Owen, it's grade four. Double high-efficiency
filtration. Negative pressure differential,

3937
05:21:19,005 --> 05:21:24,884
constant. There's a maximum-containment laboratory
under this building. It's real. It's

3938
05:21:24,904 --> 05:21:24,951
—

3939
05:21:26,472 --> 05:21:31,976
She stopped, because Carrick had turned around, and
was not looking at her. He was looking

3940
05:21:31,996 --> 05:21:35,044
past her, at the roof access door,
which was open.

3941
05:21:35,616 --> 05:21:41,444
It had been closed when they arrived. He was certain
of it. And now it was open, and the

3942
05:21:41,465 --> 05:21:47,295
stairwell behind it was lit, and at the top of the
stairs a stocky man in navy coveralls

3943
05:21:47,315 --> 05:21:51,617
with a tool belt was standing, perfectly
still, holding the door.

3944
05:21:52,306 --> 05:21:57,926
He says you can come down if you like, Agent
Carrick. Just you. Doctor Haddad can stay

3945
05:21:57,947 --> 05:21:59,041
with her machine.

3946
05:22:01,562 --> 05:22:06,260
He went. Of course he went. He had been
waiting two years to be invited.

3947
05:22:06,830 --> 05:22:13,064
In the freight elevator, standing beside Gus, he looked
at the panel. Loading dock. Basement.

3948
05:22:13,084 --> 05:22:19,048
And below them, where there had always been a blank
steel plate with four screws, a black

3949
05:22:19,068 --> 05:22:24,628
button with a thin crimson ring, glowing softly,
as if it had been there all along.

3950
05:22:25,199 --> 05:22:26,348
Gus pressed it.

3951
05:22:28,416 --> 05:22:30,389
The doors opened onto white.

3952
05:22:30,959 --> 05:22:36,359
He walked the corridor. He could not have told you
afterwards how long it took. He looked

3953
05:22:36,379 --> 05:22:41,595
into the laboratories through the glass, and saw
benches, and sequencers, and pressure

3954
05:22:41,615 --> 05:22:46,770
suits hanging like skins, and people in white coats
working at two in the morning who

3955
05:22:46,790 --> 05:22:52,007
did not look up at him as he passed. He saw an
enclosure behind thick glass where five

3956
05:22:52,027 --> 05:22:57,243
rhesus macaques sat very still, in a row, watching
him with eyes that caught the light

3957
05:22:57,263 --> 05:22:59,740
a little too brightly, and did not blink.

3958
05:23:00,310 --> 05:23:06,349
And at the end of the corridor, in front of a steel door
six inches thick, with a red-and-white

3959
05:23:06,369 --> 05:23:09,856
emblem painted on it, the Director
was waiting for him.

3960
05:23:12,047 --> 05:23:14,395
Hello, Owen. I thought it was
time you saw it.

3961
05:23:15,915 --> 05:23:22,220
He opened the steel door with a touch. Behind it, in a
cold room, stood a cryogenic cradle

3962
05:23:22,240 --> 05:23:28,334
nineteen feet tall. The produce truck had made its
long journey in reverse in February,

3963
05:23:28,354 --> 05:23:34,168
from the desert back to Delaware, and the grey
figure had been home for two months.

3964
05:23:34,737 --> 05:23:40,298
The frost cleared from the window, from the centre
outward. And Owen Carrick saw what

3965
05:23:40,318 --> 05:23:46,009
Rick Dorsey had seen, and Howard Lessing had heard,
and twelve Russian soldiers had met

3966
05:23:46,029 --> 05:23:47,454
in the dark in Nevada.

3967
05:23:48,024 --> 05:23:53,852
He did not scream. He did not run. He stood very
still for a long time, and he looked

3968
05:23:53,872 --> 05:23:59,701
at it, and the only sound in the cold room was the
slow breath of the compressor, and

3969
05:23:59,721 --> 05:24:00,665
his own heart.

3970
05:24:03,354 --> 05:24:04,347
What is it?

3971
05:24:04,865 --> 05:24:07,682
The reason nobody is ever going
to believe you.

3972
05:24:09,704 --> 05:24:11,167
Carrick drew his pistol.

3973
05:24:11,737 --> 05:24:17,216
He did not decide to. It happened the way things
happen when a mind has been stretched

3974
05:24:17,236 --> 05:24:22,716
too far for too long. He turned, and the weapon was
in his hand, and it was pointed at

3975
05:24:22,736 --> 05:24:28,536
the centre of the Director's chest from eight feet
away, and his finger was on the trigger.

3976
05:24:29,225 --> 05:24:30,503
You're under arrest.

3977
05:24:31,023 --> 05:24:31,728
For what?

3978
05:24:32,247 --> 05:24:35,172
I don't know. I don't care. I'll
think of something.

3979
05:24:36,692 --> 05:24:37,632
Go on, then.

3980
05:24:39,651 --> 05:24:40,701
He fired.

3981
05:24:41,271 --> 05:24:47,782
He fired fifteen times, until the slide locked back on
an empty magazine. He had qualified

3982
05:24:47,801 --> 05:24:54,021
as an expert marksman every year for thirteen years.
At eight feet, he could not miss.

3983
05:24:56,591 --> 05:25:02,016
When the smoke cleared, the Director was standing
exactly where he had been standing.

3984
05:25:02,037 --> 05:25:05,476
His coat was not marked. His
sunglasses were still on.

3985
05:25:06,047 --> 05:25:11,434
He held out his left hand, palm up. In it were
fifteen flattened pieces of lead.

3986
05:25:13,502 --> 05:25:19,033
He stepped forward, took Owen Carrick's right hand —
gently, the way you might take the

3987
05:25:19,052 --> 05:25:24,711
hand of a man who has fallen — turned it over, and
poured the bullets into his palm. They

3988
05:25:24,730 --> 05:25:25,348
were warm.

3989
05:25:26,038 --> 05:25:28,494
Keep those. You'll want something
to show people.

3990
05:25:31,014 --> 05:25:37,208
Carrick looked down at them. Fifteen pieces of lead
in his palm, warm, flattened like

3991
05:25:37,228 --> 05:25:42,911
coins. Behind him, in the frosted window, the
grey giant had not even stirred.

3992
05:25:45,100 --> 05:25:49,187
Let me tell you what happens now, Owen. Gus is going
to take you back up. You'll collect

3993
05:25:49,207 --> 05:25:53,386
Doctor Haddad from the roof. You'll go home to Laura.
And tomorrow morning at nine, you'll

3994
05:25:53,406 --> 05:25:57,632
learn that the Bureau's Office of Professional
Responsibility received, overnight, security

3995
05:25:57,652 --> 05:26:01,599
footage of you breaking into a private research
facility with a loaded service weapon

3996
05:26:01,619 --> 05:26:04,911
— footage in which, unlike some of my staff,
you are perfectly visible.

3997
05:26:05,312 --> 05:26:10,603
They'll also receive bank records. A numbered
account in Cyprus. The same bank Howard

3998
05:26:10,622 --> 05:26:16,165
Lessing used, when Halvorsen Pike paid him to let
four armed men into this building. Four

3999
05:26:16,185 --> 05:26:21,539
hundred thousand dollars, deposited in your name, in
twenty twenty-nine, the month you

4000
05:26:21,559 --> 05:26:22,977
opened him as a source.

4001
05:26:23,497 --> 05:26:24,542
I never —

4002
05:26:25,062 --> 05:26:29,903
I know. It won't matter. The Bureau will open an
investigation. It will take six weeks.

4003
05:26:29,923 --> 05:26:34,652
You'll be dismissed. No charges will be filed,
because Umbrella will decline to press

4004
05:26:34,672 --> 05:26:39,513
any, out of compassion for your family. It will be
in the papers. It will be a very sad

4005
05:26:39,533 --> 05:26:44,263
story, about a good agent who got too close to a
corrupt informant, and lost his way.

4006
05:26:46,283 --> 05:26:47,685
Why not just kill me?

4007
05:26:49,203 --> 05:26:55,066
Because dead, you're a martyr. People build things
on martyrs. Ruined, you're a madman

4008
05:26:55,086 --> 05:27:00,949
with a handful of bullets and a story about a
monster in a basement. Nobody listens to

4009
05:27:00,969 --> 05:27:01,426
madmen.

4010
05:27:03,447 --> 05:27:09,169
In the quiet of one skull, the old voice spoke —
very softly, and with something in it

4011
05:27:09,189 --> 05:27:10,904
that was almost amusement.

4012
05:27:11,596 --> 05:27:13,560
They listened to me.

4013
05:27:15,080 --> 05:27:21,001
Wesker did not answer it. Not aloud. But for an
instant, standing in the white corridor

4014
05:27:21,021 --> 05:27:27,011
with the ruined agent in front of him, he felt
something he had not felt in a long time,

4015
05:27:27,031 --> 05:27:28,172
and did not like.

4016
05:27:28,740 --> 05:27:29,873
It was doubt.

4017
05:27:32,063 --> 05:27:34,730
Goodbye, Owen. Give my regards to
your daughters.

4018
05:27:37,251 --> 05:27:41,713
It happened exactly as he had said. It
took six weeks, not seven.

4019
05:27:42,284 --> 05:27:48,308
The footage was clear. The bank records were
impeccable — impeccably forged, although

4020
05:27:48,328 --> 05:27:54,920
no forensic accountant the Bureau employed could ever
demonstrate how. Janet Kowal testified,

4021
05:27:54,940 --> 05:28:00,961
with visible pain, that Special Agent Carrick had
been reassigned for his own welfare

4022
05:28:00,981 --> 05:28:07,289
and had disregarded that reassignment. Samira Haddad,
suspended by the CDC the same week,

4023
05:28:07,309 --> 05:28:10,489
refused to testify against him,
and resigned.

4024
05:28:11,057 --> 05:28:17,286
Owen Carrick was dismissed from the Federal Bureau of
Investigation on the twenty-second

4025
05:28:17,306 --> 05:28:23,463
of May, twenty thirty-one, after seventeen years of
service, for conduct unbecoming. No

4026
05:28:23,484 --> 05:28:29,854
criminal charges were filed. Umbrella Life Sciences
issued a statement expressing sympathy

4027
05:28:29,875 --> 05:28:30,921
for his family.

4028
05:28:31,490 --> 05:28:37,352
He kept the fifteen bullets in a jam jar on the
kitchen windowsill. He showed them, over

4029
05:28:37,372 --> 05:28:43,099
the following year, to four journalists, two members
of Congress, a Pentagon official,

4030
05:28:43,119 --> 05:28:48,780
and a priest. Every one of them was very kind to
him, and every one of them went away

4031
05:28:48,800 --> 05:28:49,849
and did nothing.

4032
05:28:52,039 --> 05:28:53,278
Are you going to stop?

4033
05:28:55,298 --> 05:28:55,955
No.

4034
05:28:57,475 --> 05:29:01,081
Then I need you to tell me what that
means. For us. For the girls.

4035
05:29:03,101 --> 05:29:08,498
He did not have an answer. He would not have one
for a long time. Laura Carrick would

4036
05:29:08,519 --> 05:29:14,554
stay with him for three more years, out of love, and
then leave, out of love for her daughters.

4037
05:29:14,574 --> 05:29:18,506
She would never stop believing him. That
was the hardest part.

4038
05:29:21,326 --> 05:29:24,040
Assessment. Adversary broken.

4039
05:29:27,925 --> 05:29:33,968
The System called him broken. It was the System's
first real mistake about a human being.

4040
05:29:34,538 --> 05:29:40,399
Owen Carrick had been broken, it was true. And a man
who is broken does not always stay

4041
05:29:40,419 --> 05:29:46,349
in pieces. Sometimes — when the pieces are sharp
enough, and the reason is simple enough

4042
05:29:46,369 --> 05:29:52,230
— he puts himself back together around a single
idea, and becomes something that cannot

4043
05:29:52,251 --> 05:29:57,301
be broken again, because there is nothing left
in him that is not the idea.

4044
05:29:57,871 --> 05:30:03,627
He had lost his badge, his career, his pension, and,
in time, his marriage. He had kept

4045
05:30:03,647 --> 05:30:05,618
fifteen bullets and the truth.

4046
05:30:22,198 --> 05:30:28,116
Martin Sloane had waited nine months to meet the
thing in the satellite image. He was

4047
05:30:28,136 --> 05:30:33,705
a patient man. He had once waited four years in
Tbilisi for a single phone call.

4048
05:30:34,275 --> 05:30:39,917
They met in June, in the private room of a club in
Georgetown that did not have a name

4049
05:30:39,937 --> 05:30:45,513
on its door, at a table by a fire that was lit even
though it was summer, because the

4050
05:30:45,532 --> 05:30:51,241
club had been lighting it every evening since
nineteen fifty-three and saw no reason to

4051
05:30:51,261 --> 05:30:51,569
stop.

4052
05:30:52,261 --> 05:30:53,456
You know what I saw.

4053
05:30:53,977 --> 05:30:59,502
A satellite passed over Nevada in November. I
assume someone at Langley was awake.

4054
05:31:00,023 --> 05:31:05,516
Someone at Langley was very awake. Twelve heat
signatures in. One out. And a helicopter

4055
05:31:05,537 --> 05:31:09,383
that's now, I'm told, a very popular
new resident of Sinaloa.

4056
05:31:10,782 --> 05:31:14,984
I'm not going to ask you what it was. I'm not going
to ask you what else you have. I'm

4057
05:31:15,004 --> 05:31:19,304
going to tell you what I want, and then I'm going to
tell you what I'll give you for it,

4058
05:31:19,324 --> 05:31:20,873
and then you're going to decide.

4059
05:31:21,394 --> 05:31:22,483
That's refreshing.

4060
05:31:23,004 --> 05:31:25,372
I'm told you like people who don't
waste your time.

4061
05:31:27,274 --> 05:31:32,266
What I want is simple. There are things the United
States government would like to be

4062
05:31:32,287 --> 05:31:37,693
able to do, in the world, that it cannot do with its
own hands. Biological things. Defensive

4063
05:31:37,712 --> 05:31:42,883
things, mostly. Detection. Countermeasures. Vaccines
that exist before the disease does.

4064
05:31:42,903 --> 05:31:47,896
And, occasionally, other things. The kind of work
that, if a government did it, would

4065
05:31:47,916 --> 05:31:52,909
require a signature from someone elected. The kind
of work that, if a private company

4066
05:31:52,930 --> 05:31:56,626
did it, under contract, would require
only a signature from me.

4067
05:31:57,145 --> 05:31:58,247
Black contracts.

4068
05:31:58,765 --> 05:32:03,269
I prefer the term classified procurement. It
sounds so much less like a film.

4069
05:32:04,790 --> 05:32:05,858
And in exchange?

4070
05:32:06,377 --> 05:32:11,729
In exchange, the investigations stop. Not the Bureau —
the Bureau's already stopped, you've

4071
05:32:11,748 --> 05:32:16,923
seen to that. I mean the others. The ones you haven't
met yet. The Department of Defense

4072
05:32:16,943 --> 05:32:21,941
has a unit that watches for technological surprise.
So does the Department of Energy.

4073
05:32:21,961 --> 05:32:26,958
So does a very small office at the National
Security Council whose director reads the

4074
05:32:26,978 --> 05:32:32,566
same German patent reports that Julian Ashcombe does.
They're all going to find you eventually.

4075
05:32:32,586 --> 05:32:37,937
I can make sure they find you as a contractor. A
classified one. And classified contractors

4076
05:32:37,957 --> 05:32:40,299
are not investigated. They're protected.

4077
05:32:42,318 --> 05:32:47,754
The Director was silent for a while. He looked at
the fire. The Cold-Read had already

4078
05:32:47,774 --> 05:32:53,466
told him everything about Martin Sloane there was to
know: that he was telling the truth,

4079
05:32:53,486 --> 05:32:59,179
that he was not telling all of it, and that he
intended, in the long run, to own Umbrella

4080
05:32:59,199 --> 05:33:04,762
the way he owned every asset he had ever run — as a
tool, to be used and then put away.

4081
05:33:05,332 --> 05:33:10,217
That was fine. The Director intended exactly
the same thing in reverse.

4082
05:33:11,907 --> 05:33:14,118
He thinks he is buying you.

4083
05:33:14,640 --> 05:33:17,905
He is buying me. He just doesn't know
what he's paying with.

4084
05:33:18,425 --> 05:33:20,496
And what is he paying with?

4085
05:33:21,014 --> 05:33:27,100
Access. To every secret his government has about
biology. Every programme. Every laboratory.

4086
05:33:27,120 --> 05:33:33,138
Every weakness. He's going to open the door to the
house and invite me to fix the plumbing.

4087
05:33:35,038 --> 05:33:40,581
I'll need the first contract to be real, Mister
Sloane. Not a test. Something that matters.

4088
05:33:41,100 --> 05:33:41,949
It will be.

4089
05:33:42,471 --> 05:33:46,586
And I'll need you to understand that I don't
do anything I can't finish.

4090
05:33:47,105 --> 05:33:50,990
I watched the satellite, Doctor Wesker. I
understand that very well.

4091
05:33:53,010 --> 05:33:59,316
They shook hands over the fire. Sloane's grip was dry
and firm and did not hold on a moment

4092
05:33:59,336 --> 05:34:04,807
too long, and the Director, for once, did not
hold on a moment too long either.

4093
05:34:05,378 --> 05:34:11,987
It was, a historian would write decades later — in a
world that had stopped allowing historians

4094
05:34:12,007 --> 05:34:18,197
to write very much — the single most consequential
handshake of the twenty-first century.

4095
05:34:18,217 --> 05:34:22,872
At the time, it was two men in a private
club, agreeing on a price.

4096
05:34:25,442 --> 05:34:31,127
There was one more thing that had to be handled
before the handshake in Georgetown could

4097
05:34:31,147 --> 05:34:35,016
mean anything, and it was not an
agency. It was a committee.

4098
05:34:35,586 --> 05:34:41,279
In March of twenty thirty-one, the Senate Health
Committee opened hearings into the pricing

4099
05:34:41,299 --> 05:34:46,802
and supply of Aeterna. It was not a hostile
committee. Nine of its seventeen members had

4100
05:34:46,823 --> 05:34:52,327
constituents who credited the drug with a parent's
mobility. But the chair was a senator

4101
05:34:52,347 --> 05:34:57,851
from a state with no Umbrella facilities, who had
spent four years being told by her own

4102
05:34:57,871 --> 05:35:03,313
hospitals that they could not afford the one
medicine everybody wanted, and she was not

4103
05:35:03,333 --> 05:35:05,069
interested in being charmed.

4104
05:35:05,640 --> 05:35:11,462
Umbrella sent Catherine Adeyemi, not the Director.
That was deliberate and it was her

4105
05:35:11,483 --> 05:35:16,894
idea, and it was the single most effective
decision the company made that year.

4106
