people across four continents whose job

5104
07:00:58,353 --> 07:01:03,996
was to decide what the world felt about Umbrella,
and then to make the world feel it.

5105
07:01:04,016 --> 07:01:09,793
He had a corner office on the tenth floor and a
house on the Brandywine and his student

5106
07:01:09,813 --> 07:01:12,458
loans had been paid off for eight years.

5107
07:01:13,028 --> 07:01:18,450
He had also not slept properly since the ghost
video. He did not tell anyone that.

5108
07:01:20,521 --> 07:01:26,948
The idea was simple. Once a year, Umbrella would bring
its people together — not the executives,

5109
07:01:26,968 --> 07:01:32,723
not the board, not the investors, but the people.
The chemists and the drivers and the

5110
07:01:32,743 --> 07:01:38,700
nurses from the foundation clinics and the security
officers and the families. From every

5111
07:01:38,720 --> 07:01:43,872
country Umbrella worked in. In one place, on
one night, to hear the Director.

5112
07:01:44,442 --> 07:01:50,263
Tomás booked the football stadium in South
Philadelphia for the eleventh of September,

5113
07:01:50,283 --> 07:01:56,376
twenty thirty-five. Sixty-eight thousand seats.
Umbrella flew in twelve thousand employees

5114
07:01:56,396 --> 07:02:02,353
from abroad, and chartered buses for thirty thousand
from the eastern seaboard, and gave

5115
07:02:02,373 --> 07:02:05,817
free tickets to every family
member who wanted one.

5116
07:02:06,386 --> 07:02:07,422
They filled it.

5117
07:02:09,493 --> 07:02:14,945
They came in the late afternoon, in their tens of
thousands, under a clear September sky.

5118
07:02:14,965 --> 07:02:20,478
They came in white coats, some of them, because it was
a joke that had become a tradition.

5119
07:02:20,498 --> 07:02:25,950
They came with their children on their shoulders.
They came in red-and-white scarves that

5120
07:02:25,970 --> 07:02:31,238
Tomás's department had sold at cost, and they waved
them, and filmed each other waving

5121
07:02:31,258 --> 07:02:36,771
them, and posted the films, and the films were
watched, that night, by two hundred million

5122
07:02:36,791 --> 07:02:37,201
people.

5123
07:02:37,772 --> 07:02:43,200
They were happy. That is important. They were not
soldiers or zealots or a mob. They were

5124
07:02:43,220 --> 07:02:48,403
forty-one thousand people who worked for the best
employer in the world, and nineteen

5125
07:02:48,423 --> 07:02:53,605
thousand people who loved them, and they had been
given free tickets to a concert and

5126
07:02:53,625 --> 07:02:58,440
a speech and a light show, and it was a
beautiful evening, and they were happy.

5127
07:02:59,009 --> 07:03:00,941
That is always how it starts.

5128
07:03:03,013 --> 07:03:08,837
In a glass box above the fifty-yard line, Catherine
Adeyemi sat with a glass of wine she

5129
07:03:08,857 --> 07:03:14,483
did not drink, and looked down at the crowd, and
thought about a phone in her handbag

5130
07:03:14,503 --> 07:03:16,475
that she had bought with cash.

5131
07:03:17,045 --> 07:03:23,502
In the press box, among forty journalists who had been
given lanyards and free food, Hannah

5132
07:03:23,522 --> 07:03:29,623
Price sat with her laptop closed and a small, worn
spiral notebook open on the desk in

5133
07:03:29,643 --> 07:03:32,256
front of her, to a page near the end.

5134
07:03:32,826 --> 07:03:38,874
And in the parking lot outside, among the chartered
buses, a man in a plain jacket stood

5135
07:03:38,894 --> 07:03:45,078
by himself, with two private investigators from Oslo,
and listened to the stadium breathe.

5136
07:03:47,648 --> 07:03:51,520
At eight o'clock the lights went down,
and the drones went up.

5137
07:03:52,091 --> 07:03:58,389
Three thousand of them, built by the factory in
Arlington that had once belonged to Aegis

5138
07:03:58,409 --> 07:04:04,991
Dynamics, rising out of the dark behind the stadium in
a single silent cloud, and assembling,

5139
07:04:05,011 --> 07:04:11,025
a thousand feet above sixty thousand upturned
faces, into an umbrella. Red and white.

5140
07:04:11,045 --> 07:04:15,639
Eight segments. Turning slowly, like a
thing seen from far above.

5141
07:04:16,210 --> 07:04:20,690
The stadium roared. It was the first time.
It was only the beginning.

5142
07:04:22,761 --> 07:04:28,237
And then, without anyone telling them to — without an
announcement, without a cue — they

5143
07:04:28,257 --> 07:04:29,236
began to say it.

5144
07:04:29,807 --> 07:04:35,444
It started in the section where the Singapore
families were sitting, and spread, the way

5145
07:04:35,464 --> 07:04:40,974
a wave spreads in a stadium, from section to
section, until sixty thousand people were

5146
07:04:40,994 --> 07:04:44,832
standing in the dark with their right
hands on their chests.

5147
07:04:45,402 --> 07:04:51,207
We are the shelter. We do not wait for the storm. We
make the world safe for those who

5148
07:04:51,227 --> 07:04:56,965
cannot make it safe for themselves. What we learn,
we keep. What we begin, we finish.

5149
07:04:56,985 --> 07:05:01,775
Where we stand, the rain does not fall. We
are not many. We are enough.

5150
07:05:03,145 --> 07:05:04,524
We are Umbrella.

5151
07:05:07,594 --> 07:05:09,966
He walked out into the silence afterwards.

5152
07:05:10,536 --> 07:05:16,913
Alone. No music. No introduction. A single spotlight
on a single microphone in the centre

5153
07:05:16,933 --> 07:05:23,023
of a stage the size of a city block, and a man in a
black suit and sunglasses walking

5154
07:05:23,043 --> 07:05:28,415
toward it, without hurrying, while sixty
thousand people held their breath.

5155
07:05:28,984 --> 07:05:34,705
He had planned to speak for five minutes. It was in
Tomás's schedule. Five minutes, then

5156
07:05:34,725 --> 07:05:37,967
the orchestra, then the fireworks,
then the buses.

5157
07:05:40,157 --> 07:05:41,033
Good evening.

5158
07:05:43,053 --> 07:05:49,010
The roar went on for forty seconds. He let it. He
stood perfectly still at the microphone

5159
07:05:49,030 --> 07:05:55,190
with his hands at his sides, and let it wash over him
and break and die away, and he waited,

5160
07:05:55,210 --> 07:05:59,489
until the silence came back, and then he
waited a little longer.

5161
07:06:00,058 --> 07:06:05,946
Eleven seconds. Somebody in the crowd counted it out
loud. Then others did. By the ninth

5162
07:06:05,966 --> 07:06:11,920
second, the whole stadium was counting, laughing, and
at nine they cheered again, because

5163
07:06:11,940 --> 07:06:16,082
they had all seen the video, and they
were all in on the joke.

5164
07:06:16,652 --> 07:06:21,539
He smiled. He did not usually. The screens
showed it, forty feet high.

5165
07:06:23,729 --> 07:06:29,591
Nine years ago, in a building two hours down the
road from here, there were six people.

5166
07:06:29,611 --> 07:06:35,473
Six. In a building nobody visited, in a company that
was dying, doing work nobody read.

5167
07:06:35,873 --> 07:06:41,596
I told them something, in a break room, on a Friday
afternoon. I told them that every

5168
07:06:41,616 --> 07:06:47,475
great thing that has ever happened in this world
began in a room exactly like that one.

5169
07:06:47,495 --> 07:06:49,300
A room nobody was watching.

5170
07:06:50,900 --> 07:06:51,916
Look around you.

5171
07:06:54,935 --> 07:07:00,151
They looked around. Sixty thousand people, in the
dark, looked at each other. And the

5172
07:07:00,171 --> 07:07:05,572
Director felt it — the new sense, the one he had not
yet bought, the one that the System

5173
07:07:05,592 --> 07:07:10,562
would sell him that night — like the deck of a
great ship tilting under his feet.

5174
07:07:12,753 --> 07:07:17,963
Nobody is watching this room. Not the governments.
Not the newspapers. Not the men in

5175
07:07:17,983 --> 07:07:23,439
glass towers who think they run the world. They are
watching the drones, and the numbers,

5176
07:07:23,459 --> 07:07:26,332
and the share price. They are
not watching you.

5177
07:07:26,731 --> 07:07:27,656
They should be.

5178
07:07:30,176 --> 07:07:31,659
That was where it changed.

5179
07:07:32,229 --> 07:07:38,392
Tomás, in the production booth at the top of the
north stand, would try for years to find

5180
07:07:38,412 --> 07:07:44,715
the exact second on the recording, and would never be
sure. But somewhere in that sentence,

5181
07:07:44,735 --> 07:07:50,899
the rhythm changed. The voice did not get louder. It
got — the only word Tomás ever found

5182
07:07:50,919 --> 07:07:52,219
for it was — older.

5183
07:07:53,909 --> 07:07:58,000
Outside these walls, the world is a storm. You know
it. You feel it every morning when

5184
07:07:58,020 --> 07:08:02,206
you read the news. Governments that cannot build a
bridge in ten years. Parliaments that

5185
07:08:02,226 --> 07:08:06,460
argue while the water rises. Leaders who promise and
forget and promise again. Every year

5186
07:08:06,480 --> 07:08:10,523
the storm is worse, and every year the men who are
supposed to hold the umbrella hold

5187
07:08:10,543 --> 07:08:13,964
it a little lower, and a little lower, until
the rain falls on everyone.

5188
07:08:15,364 --> 07:08:16,261
Not on you.

5189
07:08:17,662 --> 07:08:19,726
Where we stand — the rain does not fall.

5190
07:08:22,246 --> 07:08:27,664
The roar was different this time. Deeper. The
Director could feel it in the stage, in

5191
07:08:27,684 --> 07:08:31,695
the soles of his feet, in his chest,
where the Prototype lived.

5192
07:08:32,265 --> 07:08:38,104
And inside him — in a room on the fourth floor of
an imaginary brick building, behind

5193
07:08:38,124 --> 07:08:44,307
a door with no name — something had stood up, and
walked to the window, and put both hands

5194
07:08:44,327 --> 07:08:45,204
on the glass.

5195
07:08:47,393 --> 07:08:52,377
They will tell you that what we are building is too
big. They will tell you that no company

5196
07:08:52,397 --> 07:08:57,271
should be this strong. They will tell you to be
afraid of us. And I want you to remember,

5197
07:08:57,291 --> 07:09:02,275
when they say it, that they said the same thing about
every good thing that was ever strong

5198
07:09:02,295 --> 07:09:03,650
enough to protect anyone.

5199
07:09:04,049 --> 07:09:05,132
We are not many.

5200
07:09:06,452 --> 07:09:08,866
And sixty thousand people answered him.

5201
07:09:09,437 --> 07:09:10,469
We are enough.

5202
07:09:13,539 --> 07:09:18,994
It began in the lower bowl, behind the stage. Three
syllables. Somebody shouted them,

5203
07:09:19,014 --> 07:09:24,405
and somebody else shouted them back, and then a
whole section, stamping on the beat.

5204
07:09:24,976 --> 07:09:26,324
Um. Brel. La.

5205
07:09:26,894 --> 07:09:33,153
It spread. It went round the stadium like fire
around the rim of a bowl. Um. Brel. La.

5206
07:09:33,173 --> 07:09:39,506
Sixty thousand voices, and a hundred and twenty
thousand feet on concrete, so loud that

5207
07:09:39,526 --> 07:09:46,078
people in the neighbourhoods of South Philadelphia a
mile away came out onto their porches

5208
07:09:46,098 --> 07:09:48,853
to listen. Um. Brel. La. Um. Brel. La.

5209
07:09:52,423 --> 07:09:57,921
He did not stop them. He stood at the microphone,
perfectly still, and let it go on.

5210
07:09:58,491 --> 07:10:00,296
This was the third threshold.

5211
07:10:00,866 --> 07:10:07,015
The first had been a parking lot, and four men, and a
dashcam. The second had been a desert,

5212
07:10:07,035 --> 07:10:12,716
and twelve men, and a thing that walked through
gunfire. This one had no bodies in it

5213
07:10:12,736 --> 07:10:18,684
at all. It was only sixty thousand happy people, on a
beautiful September night, chanting

5214
07:10:18,704 --> 07:10:20,159
the name of a company.

5215
07:10:20,730 --> 07:10:23,108
It was the most dangerous of the three.

5216
07:10:25,798 --> 07:10:26,808
Listen.

5217
07:10:28,209 --> 07:10:29,810
Listen to them.

5218
07:10:32,331 --> 07:10:38,235
The old voice was weeping. There is no other word.
Not with sorrow. With a joy so total

5219
07:10:38,255 --> 07:10:44,228
and so old that it had been waiting a hundred years
to be felt again — since beer halls,

5220
07:10:44,248 --> 07:10:50,221
and torchlit stadiums, and a crowd that had once
followed it over the edge of the world.

5221
07:10:50,790 --> 07:10:56,491
And the Wesker half of the mind, standing at the
microphone with the stadium thundering

5222
07:10:56,511 --> 07:11:02,080
around it, felt something else. Something it had
not expected, and would think about,

5223
07:11:02,100 --> 07:11:03,921
alone, for a very long time.

5224
07:11:04,491 --> 07:11:05,651
It was cold.

5225
07:11:07,842 --> 07:11:09,018
It was too easy.

5226
07:11:09,536 --> 07:11:17,311
It is always easy. That is what no one ever
understands. It is always, always easy.

5227
07:11:17,832 --> 07:11:19,316
That's what frightens me.

5228
07:11:23,466 --> 07:11:28,630
Assessment. Crowd, fanaticism.
Belief, ignited.

5229
07:11:30,850 --> 07:11:32,153
Level sixty.

5230
07:11:34,372 --> 07:11:36,818
New ability. Banner sense.

5231
07:11:42,278 --> 07:11:46,887
He bought it standing at the microphone, while
they chanted, and felt it arrive.

5232
07:11:47,457 --> 07:11:53,312
The stadium was no longer sixty thousand people. It
was one thing. A single great organism,

5233
07:11:53,332 --> 07:11:58,930
breathing, with sixty thousand hearts, and he could
feel every one of them — which were

5234
07:11:58,950 --> 07:12:04,935
burning, which were flickering, which were afraid of
the thing they were feeling and chanting

5235
07:12:04,955 --> 07:12:10,553
anyway. He could feel a nurse from Lagos in section
two-fourteen who would die for him.

5236
07:12:10,573 --> 07:12:16,429
He could feel a chemist from Cambridge in section
one-ten who was chanting because everyone

5237
07:12:16,449 --> 07:12:21,982
else was, and would remember it with shame for the
rest of her life. He could feel the

5238
07:12:22,002 --> 07:12:27,535
woman in the glass box above the fifty-yard line,
not chanting at all, holding a glass

5239
07:12:27,555 --> 07:12:33,023
of wine, and he could feel — like a cold draught
under a door — exactly how close she

5240
07:12:33,043 --> 07:12:34,056
was to breaking.

5241
07:12:36,626 --> 07:12:39,624
The world woke up to the photographs
the next morning.

5242
07:12:40,193 --> 07:12:46,141
Every front page on Earth carried the same image: a
stadium in the dark, sixty thousand

5243
07:12:46,161 --> 07:12:52,039
fists in the air, and three thousand drones in the
shape of an umbrella. The headlines

5244
07:12:52,059 --> 07:12:57,526
were different in every language. In most of
them, they asked the same question.

5245
07:12:58,097 --> 07:12:59,441
Cult, or company?

5246
07:13:01,510 --> 07:13:07,154
In the press box, long after the other journalists
had gone, Hannah Price sat alone with

5247
07:13:07,174 --> 07:13:12,819
Walter Pruitt's notebook open in front of her. She
had read it a hundred times since the

5248
07:13:12,839 --> 07:13:16,102
padded envelope had arrived with
no return address.

5249
07:13:16,674 --> 07:13:22,511
She turned to the last page he had written on. There
was room at the bottom, below his

5250
07:13:22,531 --> 07:13:28,574
blocky capitals. She took out her own pen, and wrote
beneath them, in her own small hand,

5251
07:13:28,594 --> 07:13:31,299
the date, and the place, and four words.

5252
07:13:31,867 --> 07:13:33,805
They're saying it like soldiers.

5253
07:13:35,876 --> 07:13:37,981
Then she underlined it. Twice.

5254
07:13:40,552 --> 07:13:46,643
So ended the conquest of the companies. It had taken
four years. It had cost a great deal

5255
07:13:46,663 --> 07:13:52,480
of money, and one man's mind, and a great many
people's peace. And it had made Albert

5256
07:13:52,500 --> 07:13:58,385
Wesker the master of the most powerful private
institution in the history of the human

5257
07:13:58,405 --> 07:13:58,729
race.

5258
07:14:25,593 --> 07:14:28,998
The narrator is not going to
describe the disease.

5259
07:14:29,568 --> 07:14:34,632
You have lived through one. You remember what it was
to watch a number climb on a screen,

5260
07:14:34,652 --> 07:14:39,772
and to learn the words for things you had never needed
words for, and to stand at a window

5261
07:14:39,792 --> 07:14:44,912
and see a street with nothing in it. You do not need
me to build you another. It is enough

5262
07:14:44,932 --> 07:14:49,881
to say that in the spring of twenty thirty-six a new
illness appeared in nine countries

5263
07:14:49,901 --> 07:14:54,735
in the same week, and that the world's doctors took
one look at the pattern of it and

5264
07:14:54,755 --> 07:14:57,934
understood that it had not come from
anywhere in nature.

5265
07:14:58,503 --> 07:15:05,213
They called it Pale Horse. A journalist chose the name,
from Revelation, in a Sunday newspaper,

5266
07:15:05,233 --> 07:15:09,675
and by the following weekend it was the
only name anybody used.

5267
07:15:11,747 --> 07:15:18,078
What matters, for this story, is what it did to
people. Schools closed in forty countries.

5268
07:15:18,098 --> 07:15:24,077
Borders shut. Two hundred and sixty thousand people
died in seven weeks, most of them

5269
07:15:24,097 --> 07:15:29,370
in the first six, most of them before anyone
had agreed on what to call it.

5270
07:15:29,940 --> 07:15:33,997
And on the eleventh day, Umbrella
announced that it had a vaccine.

5271
07:15:36,567 --> 07:15:43,292
Twenty-two days. From the publication of the first
genetic sequence to a finished, tested,

5272
07:15:43,312 --> 07:15:45,016
manufacturable vaccine.

5273
07:15:45,586 --> 07:15:51,440
The rapid-response platform had been built for the
Pentagon, under Martin Sloane's first

5274
07:15:51,460 --> 07:15:57,581
contract, and paid for by the American taxpayer, and it
had promised nine days and delivered

5275
07:15:57,601 --> 07:16:02,654
eight in a test. This was the first time it had
been used on something real.

5276
07:16:03,223 --> 07:16:09,016
Umbrella gave it away. That was Catherine's idea,
and Tomás's, and it was the correct

5277
07:16:09,036 --> 07:16:15,035
one, and it was also — as Catherine said in the
meeting where it was decided, in a voice

5278
07:16:15,055 --> 07:16:21,258
that made three people look at the table — the single
most profitable decision in corporate

5279
07:16:21,278 --> 07:16:27,208
history. Not one dollar for the vaccine. Cost price,
to every government on Earth, with

5280
07:16:27,228 --> 07:16:33,157
the Umbrella Foundation covering the cost for the
forty poorest countries. Four hundred

5281
07:16:33,177 --> 07:16:39,449
million doses from the plant in Singapore in the first
month, which was exactly the capacity

5282
07:16:39,469 --> 07:16:45,604
that a man had built in twenty twenty-nine and been
asked about by his own chief financial

5283
07:16:45,624 --> 07:16:49,092
officer, and had said: I believe
in being prepared.

5284
07:16:49,661 --> 07:16:55,860
By June it was over. By August the schools were open.
By the autumn of twenty thirty-six,

5285
07:16:55,880 --> 07:17:02,079
in every country on Earth, Umbrella's emblem had
stopped meaning a pharmaceutical company

5286
07:17:02,099 --> 07:17:08,089
and started meaning something closer to what it
looked like: a red-and-white umbrella,

5287
07:17:08,109 --> 07:17:09,905
held over you, in a storm.

5288
07:17:10,475 --> 07:17:16,193
The Umbrella Foundation was given the Nobel Peace
Prize the following year. The Director

5289
07:17:16,213 --> 07:17:21,735
did not attend. He sent Evelyn Marsh, who did not
speak, and stood at the back of the

5290
07:17:21,755 --> 07:17:26,755
photographs, and looked, in every one of them,
as if she were somewhere else.

5291
07:17:29,325 --> 07:17:35,090
He found out in October, five months after it
ended, and he found out by accident.

5292
07:17:35,660 --> 07:17:41,415
It was a shipping record. Not even a real one — an
internal reconciliation, one of the

5293
07:17:41,435 --> 07:17:47,256
thousands that Pell's systems generated every week
and that nobody read. It showed that

5294
07:17:47,276 --> 07:17:53,030
in the autumn of twenty thirty-five, four months
before the first case in Frankfurt, a

5295
07:17:53,050 --> 07:17:58,737
sealed container had gone from the Arklay sublevel
to the Basel vault, and from Basel

5296
07:17:58,757 --> 07:18:04,712
to three laboratories that Umbrella had acquired with
Halvorsen Pike, in three countries.

5297
07:18:05,283 --> 07:18:11,202
The three countries were not random. He looked at them
for a long time. Then he went down.

5298
07:18:13,272 --> 07:18:18,577
She did not pretend. That was the thing he would
remember. He put the page down on the

5299
07:18:18,597 --> 07:18:23,964
bench beside her, and she looked at it, and then she
looked up at him, and her face was

5300
07:18:23,984 --> 07:18:24,892
perfectly calm.

5301
07:18:25,583 --> 07:18:27,820
You weren't supposed to find that
for another year.

5302
07:18:29,840 --> 07:18:30,567
Tell me.

5303
07:18:31,086 --> 07:18:32,298
You'll want to sit down.

5304
07:18:32,819 --> 07:18:33,823
Tell me, Evelyn.

5305
07:18:36,343 --> 07:18:41,327
You built a machine that could make a cure for
anything in eight days, and you sold it

5306
07:18:41,347 --> 07:18:46,390
to the Pentagon, and it sat in a building in
Maryland doing nothing for four years. You

5307
07:18:46,410 --> 07:18:51,336
built a factory for four hundred million doses and
you told Catherine you believed in

5308
07:18:51,356 --> 07:18:56,341
being prepared. You built clinics in forty-one
countries. You built all of it, and you

5309
07:18:56,361 --> 07:18:57,097
were waiting.

5310
07:18:57,497 --> 07:18:58,672
I didn't want to wait.

5311
07:19:00,692 --> 07:19:03,018
Two hundred and sixty thousand people.

5312
07:19:03,538 --> 07:19:04,093
Yes.

5313
07:19:04,614 --> 07:19:05,511
Say the number.

5314
07:19:06,031 --> 07:19:07,995
Two hundred and sixty thousand.

5315
07:19:09,396 --> 07:19:14,399
And forty million a year from frailty and age,
before Aeterna. And nine million a year

5316
07:19:14,419 --> 07:19:19,540
from the diseases we're going to take next, now that
every government on Earth will sign

5317
07:19:19,560 --> 07:19:24,506
anything we put in front of them. I did the
arithmetic, Albert. I did it for nineteen

5318
07:19:24,526 --> 07:19:29,880
months before I did anything else. I am not a monster.
I am the only person in this building

5319
07:19:29,900 --> 07:19:31,341
who has actually counted.

5320
07:19:33,860 --> 07:19:39,587
The Cold-Read gave him her face, and it was the
worst thing it had ever given him. No

5321
07:19:39,607 --> 07:19:45,335
guilt. No fear. No doubt. Only the terrible,
luminous calm of a person who has worked

5322
07:19:45,355 --> 07:19:50,338
something out to the last decimal place and
found that it comes out right.

5323
07:19:50,910 --> 07:19:56,694
He had made her. That was the part he could not put
down. He had found a young woman in

5324
07:19:56,714 --> 07:20:02,699
a dying laboratory who had never once been seen by
anybody, and he had seen her, and shown

5325
07:20:02,719 --> 07:20:08,437
her a sleeping giant behind glass, and given her a
programme with a name, and reported

5326
07:20:08,457 --> 07:20:14,175
to nobody, and told her — over nine years, in a
hundred small ways — that the ordinary

5327
07:20:14,195 --> 07:20:16,511
rules were for the people upstairs.

5328
07:20:17,081 --> 07:20:22,471
She had listened to every word. She had simply gone
further than he had, because she was

5329
07:20:22,491 --> 07:20:26,160
younger, and because she had never had
a bunker to remember.

5330
07:20:28,730 --> 07:20:34,332
The edge of the steel bench bent under his hand. He
did not notice until afterwards.

5331
07:20:35,021 --> 07:20:36,525
You did this without orders.

5332
07:20:37,045 --> 07:20:37,600
Yes.

5333
07:20:38,119 --> 07:20:43,351
Do you understand what that means? Not morally. I
don't care about that. Do you understand

5334
07:20:43,371 --> 07:20:44,985
what it means operationally?

5335
07:20:46,384 --> 07:20:51,444
It means I did not know. For five months, the most
important thing happening on this planet

5336
07:20:51,464 --> 07:20:56,189
was happening inside my own company, and I did not
know. Every government on Earth is

5337
07:20:56,209 --> 07:21:01,046
looking for who made that, Evelyn. They will look
for years. They are better at it than

5338
07:21:01,066 --> 07:21:05,009
you think, and one of them is Wen Shulan,
and she is not going to stop.

5339
07:21:05,530 --> 07:21:06,578
They'll never find it.

5340
07:21:07,096 --> 07:21:12,388
They found the Russians in Nevada. They found the
money in Ireland. They found a smear

5341
07:21:12,408 --> 07:21:17,637
on a dashcam. They find everything eventually. The
only thing that has ever protected

5342
07:21:17,657 --> 07:21:22,083
us is that when they find it, I have already
decided what they will see.

5343
07:21:23,983 --> 07:21:26,817
You have made a fact about me that
I did not choose.

5344
07:21:29,338 --> 07:21:30,811
Let her alone.

5345
07:21:31,331 --> 07:21:32,207
Not now.

5346
07:21:32,727 --> 07:21:38,812
Listen to me. You are angry because she moved
without you. That is the only reason. Not

5347
07:21:38,832 --> 07:21:42,392
the dead. You have never once
cared about the dead.

5348
07:21:42,912 --> 07:21:44,364
I care about the variables.

5349
07:21:44,884 --> 07:21:51,886
She has just handed you the world. Every border on
this planet opened for your aircraft

5350
07:21:51,906 --> 07:21:59,473
this year. Every health ministry signs what your lawyers
write. The Foundation is in forty-one

5351
07:21:59,493 --> 07:22:06,577
countries and the people in them cheer when your
trucks arrive. In one year she has done

5352
07:22:06,597 --> 07:22:10,612
what your contracts would not have
done in twenty.

5353
07:22:11,134 --> 07:22:12,905
At a cost I did not authorise.

5354
07:22:13,425 --> 07:22:19,821
Do you know what I would have given for one officer
like her? One. Someone who understood

5355
07:22:19,841 --> 07:22:25,949
the objective so completely that they did not need
to be told. I had a continent full

5356
07:22:25,969 --> 07:22:28,040
of men who waited to be told.

5357
07:22:29,939 --> 07:22:35,976
She is the most dangerous person in your empire. She
is also the only one who has ever

5358
07:22:35,996 --> 07:22:38,230
surprised you. Do not waste her.

5359
07:22:40,749 --> 07:22:46,445
Wesker stood in the white laboratory for a long time
with his hand on a bent steel bench.

5360
07:22:47,014 --> 07:22:52,455
And the thing that frightened him — the thing he
would take out and look at, alone, in

5361
07:22:52,475 --> 07:22:57,852
the Memory Palace, for years afterwards — was not
what she had done. It was that when

5362
07:22:57,872 --> 07:23:02,234
the old voice finished speaking, he had
found that he agreed with it.

5363
07:23:04,923 --> 07:23:08,886
You will never do anything like this again
without telling me first.

5364
07:23:09,407 --> 07:23:10,454
Is that an order?

5365
07:23:10,972 --> 07:23:13,831
It's the only one I will ever give
you that matters.

5366
07:23:15,851 --> 07:23:17,068
Then I'll tell you first.

5367
07:23:18,590 --> 07:23:24,412
She meant it. That was the tragedy of Evelyn Marsh,
and it took another eighteen years

5368
07:23:24,432 --> 07:23:30,322
to finish. She never lied to him, and she never
disobeyed a direct order, and she never

5369
07:23:30,342 --> 07:23:31,341
once needed to.

5370
07:23:33,911 --> 07:23:39,848
Samira Haddad had been at the World Health
Organization for four years by then. She had

5371
07:23:39,868 --> 07:23:45,805
left the CDC after her suspension, and spent two
years in the field in three countries,

5372
07:23:45,825 --> 07:23:51,967
and been hired in Geneva by a Norwegian assistant
director-general who had read her buried

5373
07:23:51,987 --> 07:23:55,323
report from twenty thirty and
never forgotten it.

5374
07:23:55,893 --> 07:24:01,643
She ran the outbreak-origins unit. It was her job to
find out where Pale Horse had come

5375
07:24:01,663 --> 07:24:05,423
from, and she gave it everything she
had for three years.

5376
07:24:05,993 --> 07:24:11,975
She never proved it. She got close enough that she
stopped sleeping. Fifteen simultaneous

5377
07:24:11,995 --> 07:24:17,911
introductions in twenty countries is not how nature
behaves; nature starts in one place.

5378
07:24:17,931 --> 07:24:24,049
She mapped the eight. She found that all sixteen were
within forty kilometres of a facility

5379
07:24:24,069 --> 07:24:29,782
that Umbrella had acquired with Halvorsen Pike, and
she wrote that down, and then she

5380
07:24:29,802 --> 07:24:35,920
sat and looked at what she had written for a long
time, because she also knew that Umbrella

5381
07:24:35,940 --> 07:24:39,967
had facilities within forty kilometres
of almost everywhere.

5382
07:24:40,536 --> 07:24:46,330
She sent it up anyway. It went to the Director-General,
and then to the Emergency Committee,

5383
07:24:46,350 --> 07:24:51,829
and then into a process, and the process took
thirteen months, and at the end of it the

5384
07:24:51,849 --> 07:24:57,517
World Health Organization published a report which
concluded that the origin of Pale Horse

5385
07:24:57,537 --> 07:25:02,511
could not be determined with available evidence,
and recommended further study.

5386
07:25:03,081 --> 07:25:09,268
Umbrella funded the further study. Nobody found that
strange. Umbrella funded everything

5387
07:25:09,288 --> 07:25:09,833
by then.

5388
07:25:11,903 --> 07:25:18,104
Owen Carrick came to Geneva that winter. He was fifty
now, and he worked for a Norwegian

5389
07:25:18,124 --> 07:25:24,253
foundation that existed, as far as its filings
showed, to fund investigative journalism

5390
07:25:24,273 --> 07:25:25,879
in the public interest.

5391
07:25:26,447 --> 07:25:29,360
They sat on a bench outside the
building in the snow.

5392
07:25:30,051 --> 07:25:35,543
I can't prove it, Owen. I've got six dots and a
company that's within forty kilometres

5393
07:25:35,563 --> 07:25:36,954
of every dot on Earth.

5394
07:25:37,474 --> 07:25:38,346
I know.

5395
07:25:38,865 --> 07:25:44,095
And even if I could — who do I give it to? The
Security Council is four governments that

5396
07:25:44,115 --> 07:25:49,584
need his vaccines and one that needs his money. The
press won't touch it without a document.

5397
07:25:49,604 --> 07:25:50,538
And the public —

5398
07:25:51,940 --> 07:25:57,673
Owen, half the people I work with have a photograph
of their grandmother on a motorcycle.

5399
07:25:57,693 --> 07:25:59,871
Taken last year. She's ninety-one.

5400
07:26:01,890 --> 07:26:02,927
So we wait.

5401
07:26:03,446 --> 07:26:04,130
For what?

5402
07:26:04,650 --> 07:26:10,608
For him to do something he can't explain. He's never
done one yet. But he's getting bigger,

5403
07:26:10,628 --> 07:26:15,205
Samira, and the bigger a thing gets, the
harder it is to stand behind.

5404
07:26:18,355 --> 07:26:21,962
Assessment. Global dependency. Total.

5405
07:26:26,620 --> 07:26:31,217
A hundred and forty-eight governments out of
a hundred and ninety-three.

5406
07:26:31,788 --> 07:26:37,537
He read that line in a dark office, alone, in the
autumn of twenty thirty-six, and did

5407
07:26:37,557 --> 07:26:43,441
not feel triumph. He felt what a man feels when he
comes home and finds that someone has

5408
07:26:43,461 --> 07:26:49,277
tidied his house, and moved everything, and that it
is all in better places than he had

5409
07:26:49,297 --> 07:26:52,632
it, and that he no longer knows
where anything is.

5410
07:26:53,201 --> 07:26:58,508
For nine years he had been the only person in the
world who knew what the next move was.

5411
07:27:15,259 --> 07:27:19,432
Facility available. Oceanic arcology.

5412
07:27:24,198 --> 07:27:29,834
It had been in the Shop for two years. He had looked
at it the way a man looks at a house

5413
07:27:29,854 --> 07:27:33,456
he cannot yet afford, walking past it
on the way to work.

5414
07:27:34,027 --> 07:27:37,249
In the spring of twenty thirty-eight,
he could afford it.

5415
07:27:38,568 --> 07:27:40,010
Purchase confirmed.

5416
07:27:44,493 --> 07:27:48,395
The System asked him for two things.
A place, and a name.

5417
07:27:48,965 --> 07:27:55,030
The place took eleven seconds. Two hundred and forty
nautical miles west of the Azores,

5418
07:27:55,050 --> 07:28:01,045
in international waters, on a shallow seamount that
no nation had ever claimed, at the

5419
07:28:01,065 --> 07:28:05,311
intersection of three of the busiest
shipping lanes on Earth.

5420
07:28:05,882 --> 07:28:07,312
The name took longer.

5421
07:28:08,002 --> 07:28:09,817
Name it for yourself.

5422
07:28:10,337 --> 07:28:10,957
No.

5423
07:28:11,478 --> 07:28:18,649
Every founder in history has named the capital for
himself. Alexandria. Constantinople.

5424
07:28:18,669 --> 07:28:20,055
Saint Petersburg.

5425
07:28:20,574 --> 07:28:26,327
And every one of them told the world exactly what to
hate. Name a city for a man and you

5426
07:28:26,347 --> 07:28:29,214
have given his enemies a target
with a face.

5427
07:28:30,615 --> 07:28:33,112
Besides. There's only one name
it can have.

5428
07:28:35,132 --> 07:28:36,905
Arklay Free Territory.

5429
07:28:37,475 --> 07:28:43,328
It appeared over sixteen months — which is
impossible, and which the world's newspapers

5430
07:28:43,348 --> 07:28:49,471
wrote a great deal about, and for which Umbrella's
engineering division provided a complete

5431
07:28:49,491 --> 07:28:55,277
and entirely convincing explanation involving
modular construction, thirteen shipyards

5432
07:28:55,297 --> 07:29:01,286
in four countries, and a new class of deep-sea
concrete. Every element of the explanation

5433
07:29:01,306 --> 07:29:05,337
was real. Every shipyard existed. Every
contract was public.

5434
07:29:05,906 --> 07:29:11,396
The arcology itself had simply arrived, in the way
that everything from the Shop arrived,

5435
07:29:11,416 --> 07:29:15,668
and the shipyards had been building the
parts that were photographed.

5436
07:29:17,737 --> 07:29:22,474
It was, and remains, the most beautiful
thing Albert Wesker ever built.

5437
07:29:23,045 --> 07:29:29,489
Three concentric rings, four kilometres across,
rising out of the Atlantic like something

5438
07:29:29,509 --> 07:29:35,736
grown rather than made. White terraces stepped down
to the water. Farms under glass on

5439
07:29:35,756 --> 07:29:42,056
the outer ring, feeding a hundred and eighty
thousand people. A harbour that could take

5440
07:29:42,076 --> 07:29:48,521
the largest container ships afloat. Desalination,
geothermal boreholes into the seamount,

5441
07:29:48,541 --> 07:29:55,058
and a fusion-adjacent reactor whose design did not
exist anywhere else on Earth, and which

5442
07:29:55,078 --> 07:30:01,451
the International Atomic Energy Agency was invited to
inspect four times and pronounced,

5443
07:30:01,471 --> 07:30:03,920
each time, safe and unprecedented.

5444
07:30:04,491 --> 07:30:10,138
There were no cars. There were gardens on every
level, and a hospital that took anyone

5445
07:30:10,158 --> 07:30:16,003
who reached it, and schools, and a concert hall, and
six kilometres of beach made of sand

5446
07:30:16,023 --> 07:30:21,736
dredged from the seamount. The apartments were given
to employees by lottery. They were

5447
07:30:21,756 --> 07:30:22,065
free.

5448
07:30:22,635 --> 07:30:28,722
Four hundred thousand people applied to live there in
the first month. Umbrella took fourteen

5449
07:30:28,742 --> 07:30:34,764
thousand, and then twenty thousand more, and by the end
of twenty thirty-nine the population

5450
07:30:34,784 --> 07:30:40,279
was ninety-one thousand, and the waiting list was
two and a half million names long.

5451
07:30:42,849 --> 07:30:46,925
The legal question took four years and
was never really answered.

5452
07:30:47,496 --> 07:30:54,316
Arklay was not a state. Umbrella never claimed it was.
It had no flag at the United Nations,

5453
07:30:54,336 --> 07:31:01,305
no army, no currency of its own, and no citizens — only
residents, who kept whatever passports

5454
07:31:01,325 --> 07:31:07,996
they had arrived with. It was, in the careful language
of Umbrella's forty-page submission

5455
07:31:08,016 --> 07:31:14,688
to the International Maritime Organization, a
privately owned floating structure operating

5456
07:31:14,708 --> 07:31:21,231
in international waters under the flag of a small
Pacific nation that had been very glad

5457
07:31:21,251 --> 07:31:23,090
of the registration fees.

5458
07:31:23,660 --> 07:31:29,737
In practice it was a country. It had a hundred
thousand people, a police force, a court,

5459
07:31:29,757 --> 07:31:35,834
a hospital system, a school system, and a border. It
issued residency, and residency was

5460
07:31:35,854 --> 07:31:41,931
the most valuable document on Earth. And it answered
to precisely one man, who had never

5461
07:31:41,951 --> 07:31:44,218
been elected, and never would be.

5462
07:31:44,788 --> 07:31:50,917
The Security Council debated it in September. Three
of the five permanent members needed

5463
07:31:50,937 --> 07:31:57,276
Umbrella's vaccines. One needed Umbrella's investment.
The fifth was China, and the Chinese

5464
07:31:57,296 --> 07:32:03,565
ambassador, on instructions that had been drafted
personally by a deputy minister of state

5465
07:32:03,585 --> 07:32:09,505
security named Wen Shulan, gave a speech of
exquisite length about the freedom of the

5466
07:32:09,525 --> 07:32:11,391
seas, and proposed a study.

5467
07:32:11,961 --> 07:32:18,168
The study reported in twenty forty-two. By then,
Arklay had a hundred and forty thousand

5468
07:32:18,188 --> 07:32:20,433
residents and its own orchestra.

5469
07:32:23,002 --> 07:32:28,725
There was one problem on Arklay that could not be
solved by design, and it arrived in

5470
07:32:28,745 --> 07:32:31,089
the second year, in a fishing boat.

5471
07:32:31,660 --> 07:32:37,325
Four hundred kilometres of open Atlantic is not a
barrier to people who have decided to

5472
07:32:37,345 --> 07:32:42,944
leave somewhere. By twenty forty, boats had begun to
come — from West Africa, from the

5473
07:32:42,964 --> 07:32:48,956
Canaries, from wherever the storms and the economics
were worst — because the most beautiful

5474
07:32:48,976 --> 07:32:54,837
city in the world was sitting in international waters
and there was a persistent, entirely

5475
07:32:54,857 --> 07:32:58,170
false rumour that anyone who
reached it could stay.

5476
07:32:58,740 --> 07:33:05,072
The first boat had nineteen people on it. The
Umbrella Security Service took them aboard,

5477
07:33:05,092 --> 07:33:11,211
fed them, treated four for dehydration, and held
them in a facility on the fourth ring

5478
07:33:11,231 --> 07:33:15,637
that was clean and well-run and was,
unmistakably, a facility.

5479
07:33:17,706 --> 07:33:20,963
And then the Directorate had to
decide what it was.

5480
07:33:21,533 --> 07:33:27,877
A country would have had a law. Arklay was not a
country. It had no immigration statute,

5481
07:33:27,897 --> 07:33:34,602
because it had no legislature, because its entire legal
existence was a forty-page submission

5482
07:33:34,622 --> 07:33:41,182
to the International Maritime Organization describing
a privately owned floating structure.

5483
07:33:41,752 --> 07:33:47,794
Catherine argued for repatriation with compensation,
because it was defensible. The Security

5484
07:33:47,814 --> 07:33:53,459
Service argued for interception at range, because it
was simple. Evelyn, who was asked

5485
07:33:53,479 --> 07:33:59,389
because she was asked about everything by then, said
that they should be offered residency

5486
07:33:59,409 --> 07:34:05,186
on the same terms as everyone else, and when
Catherine pointed out that this would bring

5487
07:34:05,206 --> 07:34:10,128
four million people to the sea wall within a
decade, Evelyn said: yes. And?

5488
07:34:12,197 --> 07:34:18,172
The Director decided it himself, in nine minutes,
and the policy he wrote has not been

5489
07:34:18,192 --> 07:34:20,262
amended in four hundred years.

5490
07:34:20,953 --> 07:34:26,053
Anyone who reaches the sea wall alive is taken
aboard, treated, fed, and offered passage

5491
07:34:26,073 --> 07:34:31,405
to any port they choose, at our cost, with four
thousand dollars. Anyone who wants residency

5492
07:34:31,425 --> 07:34:36,583
joins the waiting list at the position they would
have had if they had applied from home.

5493
07:34:36,603 --> 07:34:40,773
No exceptions, no queue-jumping, and no boat
is ever turned back at sea.

5494
07:34:42,172 --> 07:34:46,740
And publish it. In full. Everywhere. Including
the part about the waiting list.

5495
07:34:48,759 --> 07:34:54,576
It was the most humane migration policy on Earth in
twenty forty, and it was designed,

5496
07:34:54,596 --> 07:35:00,480
deliberately and explicitly, to be exactly generous
enough that no serious person could

5497
07:35:00,500 --> 07:35:06,384
attack it and exactly strict enough that the boats
would stop coming within four years.

5498
07:35:06,954 --> 07:35:12,529
The boats stopped coming within four years. Two and
a half million people stayed on the

5499
07:35:12,549 --> 07:35:18,187
waiting list instead, in their own countries,
working, applying annually, hoping — which

5500
07:35:18,207 --> 07:35:23,846
was worth more to the Directorate than any of them
could have been as residents, because

5501
07:35:23,866 --> 07:35:27,126
a person on a waiting list is a
person who behaves.

5502
07:35:30,196 --> 07:35:35,792
Catherine Adeyemi came out for the opening of the
concert hall, and stayed for a week,

5503
07:35:35,812 --> 07:35:38,078
and it was the week that broke her.

5504
07:35:38,648 --> 07:35:44,353
It was not the arcology. The arcology was
extraordinary, and she said so publicly, and

5505
07:35:44,373 --> 07:35:50,277
meant it. It was not the schools, which were the best
she had ever seen, or the hospital,

5506
07:35:50,297 --> 07:35:56,136
which took anyone. It was the fourth morning, on the
promenade, at about seven, when she

5507
07:35:56,156 --> 07:35:57,401
went out for a run.

5508
07:35:57,970 --> 07:36:03,896
There were perhaps four hundred people out running.
That was not strange; it was a beautiful

5509
07:36:03,916 --> 07:36:07,838
morning. What was strange was that they
were running in step.

5510
07:36:08,407 --> 07:36:14,260
Nobody had organised it. There was no instructor, no
music, no app. Four hundred people

5511
07:36:14,280 --> 07:36:20,268
of different ages and different countries, out for a
private run at seven in the morning,

5512
07:36:20,288 --> 07:36:26,141
had fallen into the same stride, the way soldiers
do, and were going around the ring of

5513
07:36:26,161 --> 07:36:31,811
the city together in a long loose column, and none
of them appeared to have noticed.

5514
07:36:32,382 --> 07:36:37,709
She stopped running. She stood at the rail with her
hands on her knees and watched them

5515
07:36:37,729 --> 07:36:40,106
go past. And she looked at their faces.

5516
07:36:40,675 --> 07:36:46,271
They were happy. That was the worst of it. They
were perfectly, genuinely happy — the

5517
07:36:46,291 --> 07:36:51,887
loose, uncomplicated happiness of people who have a
good job and a free apartment and

5518
07:36:51,907 --> 07:36:57,766
