5905
08:09:59,912 --> 08:10:02,093
She sat in the chair for a long time.

5906
08:10:02,664 --> 08:10:08,254
She understood, sitting there, that she had not been
caught. She had been kept. That he

5907
08:10:08,274 --> 08:10:13,993
had known for nine years, and had let her go on
believing that she was a spy in the house

5908
08:10:14,013 --> 08:10:19,667
of a monster, because a spy who believes she is free
is more honest than a prisoner, and

5909
08:10:19,687 --> 08:10:21,021
he needed her honest.

5910
08:10:21,592 --> 08:10:27,537
She was fifty-one years old. She had been his chief
financial officer for fifteen years.

5911
08:10:27,557 --> 08:10:33,435
She had a hundred and eighty million dollars, four
homes, and a seat at the table where

5912
08:10:33,455 --> 08:10:34,927
the world was decided.

5913
08:10:35,497 --> 08:10:41,506
And she understood, in a hotel suite in Basel, with
his torn coat on the back of a chair,

5914
08:10:41,526 --> 08:10:47,400
that she was the most thoroughly owned human being
in his entire empire — because every

5915
08:10:47,420 --> 08:10:53,294
single one of the others was owned by something that
had been done to them, and she had

5916
08:10:53,314 --> 08:10:58,240
done it to herself, one reasonable decision
at a time, for fifteen years.

5917
08:11:01,429 --> 08:11:02,827
I want to resign.

5918
08:11:03,348 --> 08:11:04,242
No, you don't.

5919
08:11:24,494 --> 08:11:30,323
The Basel bomb did what Julian Ashcombe had said it
would do. It made Albert Wesker do

5920
08:11:30,343 --> 08:11:33,248
