6985
09:45:38,828 --> 09:45:44,649
But standing at that window, looking at a sky with
something working in it, Albert Wesker

6986
09:45:44,669 --> 09:45:49,439
found that he wanted, very much, to turn to
somebody and say: do you see?

6987
09:45:52,010 --> 09:45:57,901
And he did turn. Physically. In an empty observation
deck, at four in the morning, three

6988
09:45:57,921 --> 09:46:03,611
hundred kilometres above the Earth, an
eighty-year-old man in a black coat turned his

6989
09:46:03,631 --> 09:46:08,381
